:: Arcology Invite
<<effects>>
<<set $xchange.arcology.invited to true>>
They turn towards the town. "You have five million pounds and more... but you're still here. With that much money, perhaps you could use a little fresh air. Have you thought about leaving for a while?"
<br><br>
They pause, then speak again. "I was thinking of asking you to come with me. To where I come from, I mean. There's a city out there. I think you'd enjoy a look around."
<br><br>
They look across the water, and you turn to see what they are looking at. You can see only the sea and the horizon.
<br><br>
"You'd be my guest. That gets you through the gate and keeps most people polite." They turn back to you. "The ship is comfortable, but you'll have to put up with my company the whole way. Think about it, if you like."
<br><br>
<<link [[Go with them|Arcology Invite Accept]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Not yet|Arcology Invite Postpone]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Invite Postpone
<<effects>>
You tell them you aren't ready yet.
<br><br>
"That's fine," they say, leaning back against the railing. "Come and find me when you are.
And try not to get yourself into the newspapers before then. I'd rather the people at the gate didn't recognise you."
<br><br>
<<socialiseicon "ask">><<link [[Ask something else|Silver Stranger]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Docks]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Invite Accept
<<effects>><<speechresolve>>
<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
	<<case "meek">>
		"I... I'll come," you say. "If you're sure it's all right."
	<<case "shy">>
		You nod before you manage the words. "Okay. I'll come."
	<<case "polite">>
		"I'd like to see it," you say. "Thank you for asking me."
	<<case "confident">>
		"Let's go," you say. "I want to see what you've been hiding."
	<<case "bratty">>
		"Fine. But if it's boring, I'm swimming back."
	<<case "docile">>
		"Whatever you think is best," you say. "I'll go where you take me."
	<<case "flamboyant">>
		"A secret city? Of course I'm coming. Try and stop me." You smile.
	<<case "cruel">>
		You scoff. "Fine. Don't waste my time with it."
	<<default>>
		"All right," you say. "Show me."
<</switch>>
<br><br>
"I was hoping you'd say that." They push away from the railing and lead you around the cargo stacks, past workers loading crates onto a lorry. "Stay close. The boat leaves when I get on it."
<br><br>
A narrow black launch is tied up at the last post. They walk straight towards it without checking that you're following, and you pick your way after them between ropes and stacked cargo. The pilot waits at the controls and doesn't look up.
<br><br>
Several dock workers have a clear view of the boat, but nobody calls out or asks where you're going.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Voyage Board]]>><<set $xchange.arcology.voyage to { to: "arcology", escort: "luchifen", next: "Arcology Arrival 1" }>><<pass 3>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Arrival 1
<<effects>>
<<LuName>> calls you to the front of the boat. You look back towards the ship you came from,
but the thick mist makes it impossible to see. All you can see now is the sea around you.
<br><br>
The pilot begins to slow down as a row of lights appears ahead.
<br><br>
As you get closer, you make out a huge transparent dome with an entire city beneath it.
Tall buildings reach almost to the top of it, and it is so wide that you can barely see the far side.
<br><br>
Then you notice something even stranger. The whole island... is moving.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Arrival 1.1]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Arrival 1.1
<<effects>>
Beneath the buildings, you can see a huge white base floating on the water.
The entire city is moving slowly across the sea, pushing waves out to either side.
<br><br>
As the launch gets closer, you begin to see more of the city through the dome.
<br><br>
Tall buildings stand close together, with long lines of white and blue lights on their outside walls,
going from the bottom of each building to the top. Small drones fly between them,
while some of the upper floors have large glass windows that let you see trees and gardens inside.
<br><br>
Closer to the water, the buildings are older and much smaller. They are crowded together beneath the taller buildings,
with orange lights coming from their windows and the narrow streets below.
<br><br>
Near the docks, large cranes are busy loading and unloading containers from ships.
You look around for the workers controlling them, but there doesn't seem to be anyone operating the machines.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Arrival 1.2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Arrival 1.2
<<effects>>
"People do like to keep the upper levels looking nice," <<luName>> says beside you. "Down near the water, though? That rather depends on how much money you're willing to spend."
<br><br>
They smile as they watch the city dome come closer, clearly pleased to be showing it to you.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Arrival 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Arrival 2
<<location "arcology_pier">><<effects>>
<<if !$NPCList[0] or $NPCList[0].role isnot "technician">><<arcologyNPC 0 "staff" "technician">><</if>><<person1>>
The launch stops beside a long white pier.
<br><br>
At the entrance, two guards wearing grey armour stand beside a gate, their faces hidden behind dark visors.
A scanner above the gate shines a blue light over each person passing through.
<br><br>
<<LuName>> walks straight towards the guards, and you follow close behind. One guard steps forward to stop you, then sees who you are with and moves aside again. Beside the gate, a clerk in a small glass booth sees you coming and slides the window open.
<br><br>
"Guest?" the clerk asks, looking at you.
<br><br>
"Mine," <<luName>> replies. "A basic interface and a guest profile, please. Charge everything to my account. I'd like it done today."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Arrival 2.1]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Arrival 2.1
<<effects>><<person1>>
The clerk points you towards a side door near the gate. It opens onto a small white room, where a padded chair stands beside a table covered with medical equipment.
<br><br>
A <<person>> in a grey uniform is waiting by the table. <<arcologyCyberLook 0>>
<br><br>
The technician picks up a small metal device and shows it to you. "The interface goes in just behind your ear. Take a seat and keep your head still."
<br><br>
You sit down and turn your head to one side. The technician brushes your hair back from your ear, then presses the cold tip of the device against the skin behind it. There is a sharp sting, followed by a strange pressure that spreads down the side of your neck.<<pain 5>><<gpain>>
<br><br>
Before you can ask what is happening, everything turns white.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Arrival 2.2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Arrival 2.2
<<effects>>
A second later, the room comes back. Now, though, a thin blue ring sits around the edge of your vision, and several lines of text appear in the air in front of your eyes.
<br><br>
You turn your head to look around the room, but the text stays in front of you.
The technician carries on putting the equipment away and doesn't seem to see any of it.
<br><br>
<<holo "INTERFACE / FIRST BOOT">>
	<<holoRow "MODEL" "BASIC CIVILIAN INTERFACE">>
	<<holoRow "SPONSOR" "[ENCRYPTED]">>
	<<holoLine "INTERFACE ONLINE" "ok">>
	<<holoLine "DIGITAL ID: NOT REGISTERED" "warn">>
<</holo>>
<br>
"It'll itch for a day," the technician says. "Don't scratch it. Next."
<<if !$xchange.arcology.implant>>
	<<set $xchange.arcology.implant to { model: "basic", fitted: Time.date.timeStamp }>>
	<<stress 4>><<gstress>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Arrival Handle]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Arrival Handle
<<effects>>
<<LuName>> is waiting for you outside the gate, leaning against the railing.
The spot behind your ear still stings.<<gpain>><<pain 2>>
<br><br>
As you walk towards them, a new message opens in front of your eyes.
<br>
<<holo "CIVIC REGISTRY" "pending">>
	<<holoLine "ENTER A HANDLE TO REGISTER YOUR GUEST ID" "warn">>
<</holo>>
<br>
"Don't use your real name," they say, watching your eyes move over the text. "People here go by names they've chosen for themselves. You'll need one too, so pick something you like."
<br><br>
You ask why everyone needs a different name.
<br><br>
"Well, you know about X-Change, don't you? Back in town, people take those pills to change their bodies.
Some only want to try being someone else for a little while, while others prefer their new bodies and keep using them."
<br><br>
They look towards the people entering the city before continuing.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Arrival Handle 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Arrival Handle 2
<<effects>>
"Here, you can take that a little further. You can register your new body under a completely different name.
Imagine someone back on the mainland trying to find you. Your old face and your real name
wouldn't help anybody recognise you here."
<br><br>
They smile and point towards the people passing through the gate.
<br><br>
"See all these people? Some of them used to be famous. Others came here to leave their old lives behind. That's why we use these names. The registry knows who you are on the island, and nobody here needs to know who you were before."
<br><br>
You look at <<luName>>, wondering whether the person standing beside you might have changed their body too.
<br><br>
They notice you looking at them and smile.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Arrival Handle 3]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Arrival Handle 3
<<effects>>
"Now you're wondering whether I've done the same, aren't you?" they ask. "Well, perhaps I have. Perhaps the person you're looking at isn't who you think they are."
<br><br>
They laugh quietly, clearly enjoying your curiosity, but offer no further explanation.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Arrival Register]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Arrival Register
<<effects>>
<<holo "CIVIC REGISTRY / NEW GUEST" "pending">>
	<<holoLine "ENTER A HANDLE TO REGISTER YOUR GUEST ID" "warn">>
	<<holoRow "FORMAT" "3 TO 16 CHARACTERS: LETTERS, NUMBERS, . - _">>
	<label class="holo-field">HANDLE <<textbox "_arcologyHandleInput" "">></label>
<</holo>>
<br>
<<link "Register" "Arcology Arrival Register Check">><<set $xchange.arcology.handleDraft to String(_arcologyHandleInput or "").trim()>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Arrival Register Check
<<effects>>
<<set _arcologyHandleTry to $xchange.arcology.handleDraft or "">>
<<unset $xchange.arcology.handleDraft>>
<<if _arcologyHandleTry.toLowerCase() is "luchifen">>
	<<holo "CIVIC REGISTRY" "denied">>
		<<holoLine "THAT HANDLE IS ALREADY REGISTERED" "denied">>
	<</holo>>
	<br>
	Beside you, <<luName>> looks very pleased with themself.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Try another|Arcology Arrival Register]]>><</link>>
<<elseif /^[A-Za-z0-9_.\-]{3,16}$/.test(_arcologyHandleTry)>>
	<<set $xchange.arcology.handle to _arcologyHandleTry>>
	<<holo "CIVIC REGISTRY">>
		<<holoRow "HANDLE" `$xchange.arcology.handle`>>
		<<holoRow "CLEARANCE" "GUEST">>
		<<holoLine `"GUEST ID REGISTERED. WELCOME, " + $xchange.arcology.handle.toUpperCase() + "."` "ok">>
	<</holo>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Next|Arcology Arrival Name]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<holo "CIVIC REGISTRY" "denied">>
		<<holoLine "HANDLE REJECTED" "denied">>
		<<holoRow "FORMAT" "3 TO 16 CHARACTERS: LETTERS, NUMBERS, . - _">>
	<</holo>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Try another|Arcology Arrival Register]]>><</link>>
<</if>>
<br>

:: Arcology Arrival Name
<<effects>><<speechresolve>>
"<<arcologyHandle>>," <<luName>> repeats. "Well, that's the name people will know you by here."
<br><br>
<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
	<<case "meek">>
		"Um... what should I call you?" you ask.
	<<case "shy">>
		You glance at them before asking, "And what's your name?"
	<<case "polite">>
		"May I ask what I should call you?" you say.
	<<case "confident">>
		"And you? What name do you use here?" you ask.
	<<case "bratty">>
		"I've picked my name. Are you going to tell me yours?" you ask.
	<<case "docile">>
		"What would you like me to call you?" you ask.
	<<case "flamboyant">>
		"And what should I call you?" you ask with a smile.
	<<case "cruel">>
		You glance at them. "You know my name now. Tell me yours."
	<<default>>
		"What should I call you?" you ask.
<</switch>>
<br><br>
<<LuName>> smiles at the question, but doesn't answer straight away. They look out towards the city for a moment before turning back to you.
<br><br>
"Luchifen," they say at last. "That'll do. It's a handle too, before you ask."
They push away from the railing. "Come on. I'd like to get you a room before you think of another question."
<<set $xchange.silverStranger.nameKnown to true>><<npc Luchifen>>
<br><br>
<span class="gold">You now know them as</span> <<silverName>>.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Arrival Hotel]]>><<pass 15>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Arrival Hotel
<<effects>>
Luchifen leads you away from the pier and onto Relay Street. The street is busy,
with people walking past in long coats and visors. You notice that nearly everyone has a small light behind one ear.
<br><br>
Large screens cover the walls of the buildings. The adverts on them change when you look at them, and a few show your new handle for a second or two before they move on to something else.
<br><br>
Along the pavement, food stalls sell noodles and grilled meat under bright lights, with steam rising from the pots. As you pass a noodle stall, the seller sees Luchifen and stops serving to watch you both go by. Further along, two security guards in grey uniforms step out of the way before Luchifen reaches them.
<br><br>
Luchifen walks on without paying either of them any attention.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Arrival Hotel 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Arrival Hotel 2
<<effects>>
You soon pass a set of stairs leading down to a lower part of the city. The streets down there are darker, with far fewer lights than the one you're walking along.
<br><br>
Two people stand near the stairs, smoking. Both have guns attached to their belts, clearly visible to anyone passing by.
<br><br>
"Don't go down there," Luchifen says, without slowing. "Your guest key only opens this street and your hotel room. If you find a door that won't open for you, I'd leave it alone."
<br><br>
They give you a brief smile before continuing down the street.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Arrival Hotel 3]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Arrival Hotel 3
<<effects>>
A little farther along, Luchifen stops outside a tall building with a curved glass front.
<br><br>
Above the entrance, a large sign reads <span class="blue">HOTEL MERIDIAN</span>.
<br><br>
You follow Luchifen through the entrance and into the hotel lobby.
The clerk behind the reception desk notices them immediately and stands up before you even reach the desk.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Arrival Hotel 4]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Arrival Hotel 4
<<location "arcology_hotel">><<effects>>
<<if $xchange.arcology.guest.status isnot "sponsored">>
	<<run setup.arcology.scheduleParty()>>
	<<set $xchange.arcology.guest to { status: "sponsored", sponsor: "Luchifen", until: $xchange.arcology.party.end + 10 * 3600 }>>
<</if>>
The clerk turns the desk screen towards you. As soon as you look at it, the same page opens in front of your eyes through your new interface.
<br><br>
<<arcologyGuestPanel>>
<br>
"I've arranged a room for you, and I'll cover it until the party," Luchifen says. "After that, you pay for your own stay. Oh, and don't expect anyone to take pounds here. You'll need the city's own currency."
<br><br>
"What party?" you ask.
<br><br>
Luchifen smiles and takes a black card from their coat. They hold it up between two fingers, and your interface reads it before you can. An invitation opens in front of your eyes.
<br><br>
<<holo "INVITATION / THE GLASSHOUSE" "pending">>
	<<holoRow "EVENT" "MASQUERADE BALL">>
	<<holoRow "OPENS" `setup.arcology.when($xchange.arcology.party.at).toUpperCase()`>>
	<<holoRow "DOORS CLOSE" `setup.arcology.when($xchange.arcology.party.end).toUpperCase()`>>
	<<holoRow "GUEST OF" "LUCHIFEN">>
<</holo>>
<br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Arrival Hotel 5]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Arrival Hotel 5
<<effects>>
"Hmm. This is the real reason I brought you here," Luchifen says, looking rather pleased.
<br><br>
"There's a party at the Glasshouse, and some of the richest people in the city will be there. Everyone wears a mask, of course. Some of them will even pretend not to know each other, though they've met plenty of times before."
<br><br>
They give you a small smile.
<br><br>
"I thought you might enjoy seeing them for yourself. Besides, I'd rather you learned who's who before any of them start taking an interest in you."
<br><br>
They tap the card, and the invitation in front of your eyes flickers.
<br><br>
"<span class="purple">Meet me at the Glasshouse lift on Relay Street</span>. I'll be there an hour before the doors open, so you won't have to find your way in alone."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Arrival Hotel 6]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Arrival Hotel 6
<<effects>>
"Do I have to go?" you ask.
<br><br>
They slide the card back into their coat. "Nobody is going to drag you there. I'd still like you to come, though."
<br><br>
They pause, then add, "Oh, and promise me something. Until the party, keep to the streets with plenty of lights. There are parts of this city I'd rather you didn't wander into alone."
<br><br>
<<link [[Promise|Arcology Arrival End]]>><<set $phase to "promise">><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Make no promises|Arcology Arrival End]]>><<set $phase to "refuse">><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Arrival End
<<effects>><<set $xchange.arcology.arrived to true>>
<<earnFeat "An Island Invitation">><<unset $xchange.arcology.invited>>
<<set $xchange.arcology.clearance to "guest">>
<<if $phase is "promise">>
	You promise to keep to the lit streets.
	<br><br>
	"Wonderful." Luchifen smiles. "Just remember that your guest key only opens certain doors. Stay out of the places it doesn't, and we'll get along nicely."
<<else>>
	You tell them you won't make any promises.
	<br><br>
	Luchifen laughs softly. "I thought you might say that. Well, I won't stop you getting into trouble, but do try to come back from it in one piece. I'm rather curious to see what you'll do here."<<npcincr Luchifen love 1>><<glove>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
Luchifen steps away from the desk and gives you another smile. "Now, get some rest, <<arcologyHandle>>. I'll see you at the lift."
<br><br>
You start to reply, but Luchifen is already walking across the lobby. The glass doors slide open as they approach,
and they leave without slowing down.
<br><br>
<span class="gold">Your journal map has changed.</span>
<br><br>
<<link [[Go to your room|Arcology Hotel Room]]>><<endevent>><<set $phase to 0>><</link>>
<br>

/* PARTY */
:: Arcology Party Lift
<<location "arcology">><<effects>><<endevent>><<npc Luchifen>>
<<if !setup.arcology.partyOpen()>>
	The lift doors stay shut. Nobody is waiting beside them.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Back to Relay Street|Arcology Street]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<<else>>
	Luchifen is waiting beside the glass lift in a long black coat with silver thread at the cuffs. They are holding two masks by their ribbons, one white and one black, and swinging them gently.
	<br><br>
	"You came." They sound pleased, and a little surprised, though you suspect the surprise is for your benefit.
	<<if playerHasXChangeBody()>>
		Luchifen takes a closer look at your face and smiles. "X-Changed, even. That should make introductions easier."
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Go up with them|Arcology Party Enter]]>><<pass 10>><</link>>
		<br>
	<<else>>
		They stop swinging the masks. "Before we go up. You walked across this island in your own face. That's fine on Relay Street. Upstairs, some of the guests have long memories and better cameras than the city does."
		<br><br>
		They take a small flat case out of their coat and open it. There is a single X-Change pill inside.
		"It's yours if you want it. Free, before you ask. Most people up there have taken one themselves. Of course, whether they'll admit that to you is another matter."
		<br><br>
		<<if xchangeCanStartTransform("pink") or xchangeCanStartTransform("blue")>>
			<<link [[Take the pill|Arcology Party Pill]]>><</link>>
			<br>
			<<link [[Keep it for later|Arcology Party Keep]]>><<set $sexStats.pills.pills[xchangeCanStartTransform("pink") ? "X-Change Pink Weekly" : "X-Change Blue Weekly"].owned += 1>><<set $sexStats.pills.boughtOnce to true>><</link>>
			<br>
		<<else>>
			<span class="purple"><<print xchangeTransformBlockedReason(xchangeCanStartTransform("pink") ? "pink" : "blue")>></span>
			<br>
			"Ah." Luchifen closes the case. "Then you'll go as you are."
			<br><br>
		<</if>>
		<<link [[Go as you are|Arcology Party Decline]]>><</link>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
	<<link [[Tell them you aren't going|Arcology Party Refuse Confirm]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Arcology Party Pill
<<effects>>
You take the pill from the case and swallow it while Luchifen watches with a small smile.
<br><br>
<<if xchangeCanStartTransform("pink")>>
	<<xchange-pink 7>>
<<elseif xchangeCanStartTransform("blue")>>
	<<xchange-blue 7>>
<</if>>
Your stomach starts to feel hot, and the heat soon spreads to your arms and legs. Your bones begin to ache, followed by an uncomfortable feeling in your skin as your body changes.
You grab the rail beside the lift to keep your balance until the pain finally stops.
<br><br>
You look down at yourself. Your clothes fit differently now, and even your hands look unfamiliar. You move your fingers a little, getting used to seeing them like this.
<br><br>
"Well, look at you," Luchifen says. "Now you're a stranger too. Welcome."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Party Enter]]>><<pass 10>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Party Keep
<<effects>>
You take the pill out of its case and look at it for a moment before putting it back. You decide to save it for another time.
<br><br>
"Saving it for later? That's your choice. You'll be attending the party in your own body tonight, then."
They hold up the white mask by its ribbon.
"You'll wear this until midnight. And if anyone asks whether you've met them before, you don't have to answer."
<br><br>
<span class="gold">You have an X-Change Weekly</span> pill in your pill case.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Party Enter]]>><<pass 10>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Party Decline
<<effects>>
You tell Luchifen that you'd rather attend the party in your own body.
<br><br>
"As you wish." Luchifen closes the case and puts it back inside their coat, then holds up the white mask.
"Just make sure you wear this until midnight. And if somebody asks whether you've met, you don't owe them an answer."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Party Enter]]>><<pass 10>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Party Refuse Confirm
<<effects>>
<<speechresolve>>
<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
	<<case "meek">>
		"I'm sorry, but I don't want to go to the party," you say.
	<<case "shy">>
		You look towards the lift, then back at Luchifen. "I don't think I can go to the party. Sorry."
	<<case "polite">>
		You look towards the lift, then back at Luchifen. "Thank you for inviting me, but I'd rather not go to the party."
	<<case "confident">>
		You look towards the lift, then back at Luchifen. "I've made up my mind. I'm not going to the party."
	<<case "bratty">>
		You look towards the lift, then back at Luchifen. "I'm not going to your bloody party. Forget it."
	<<case "docile">>
		You look towards the lift, then back at Luchifen. "I'm sorry. I know you wanted me to come, but I don't want to go."
	<<case "flamboyant">>
	You look towards the lift, then back at Luchifen. "Thank you for the invitation, but I'll have to miss the party."
	<<case "cruel">>
		You look towards the lift, then back at Luchifen. "I'm not going. Find someone else to entertain your guests."
	<<default>>
		You look towards the lift, then back at Luchifen. "I've decided not to go to the party."
<</switch>>
<br><br>
Luchifen lowers the two masks they are holding. They look at you for a moment, then ask if you've thought about what you're saying.
"You came all this way for the party. Are you sure you want to leave without attending?"
<br><br>
Luchifen invited you to the island for this party. If you refuse to attend, <span class="red">you won't be allowed to stay on the island.</span>
<br><br>
<<link [[Refuse|Arcology Party Failed]]>><<set $xchange.arcology.party.why to "refused">><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Change your mind|Arcology Party Lift]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Party Enter
<<location "arcology_glasshouse">><<effects>>
<<if setup.arcology.partyMissed()>>
	<<set $xchange.arcology.party.why to "missed">>
	<<include "Arcology Party Failed">>
<<else>>
	<<set $xchange.arcology.party.status to "attending">>
	<<if !$xchange.arcology.party.seen.includes("mask")>>
		<<set $xchange.arcology.party.xchanged to playerHasXChangeBody()>>
		<<if !$xchange.arcology.party.xchanged>><<run setup.arcology.expose(2)>><</if>>
	<</if>>
	The lift moves up the outside of the tower, giving you a view of the city below. As you get higher, the streets become smaller and their lights look like thin lines. You can also see the sea beyond the city.
	<br><br>
	When the lift reaches the top, you find a guard in a white suit standing beside a glass door. As you approach, a screen appears on the door, showing your guest information. The guard waits while the system checks your identity.
	<br><br>
	<<holo "GLASSHOUSE / DOOR">>
		<<holoRow "GUEST" `$xchange.arcology.handle`>>
		<<holoRow "INVITED BY" "LUCHIFEN">>
		<<if $xchange.arcology.party.xchanged>>
			<<holoRow "FACE MATCH" "NO RECORD">>
		<<else>>
			<<holoRow "FACE MATCH" "SEARCHING EXTERNAL RECORDS...">>
		<</if>>
		<<holoLine "ENTRY GRANTED" "ok">>
	<</holo>>
	<br>
	Once your entry is approved, Luchifen lends you a smooth white half-mask with white ribbons for the party, keeping the black one for themselves. <<specialClothesUnlock "set" "luchifen_mask">>
	<<if !$xchange.arcology.party.seen.includes("maskWorn")>>
		<<run $xchange.arcology.party.seen.push("maskWorn")>>
		<<if $worn.face.cursed is 1>>
			You can't remove your current face covering, so you carry the party mask instead.
		<<elseif $worn.face.name isnot "white half-mask">>
			<<facewear "white half-mask">><<set $worn.face.borrowed to true>>
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
	<<if !$xchange.arcology.party.seen.includes("mask")>>
		<<run $xchange.arcology.party.seen.push("mask")>>
	<</if>>
	<<run updateMoment()>>
	<br><br>
	<<if $worn.face.name is "white half-mask">>"Tie the ribbon behind your head," they say, showing you how to wear it. "And don't take the mask off until everyone else takes theirs off."<<else>>Luchifen glances at the mask in your hand. "Keep it with you. The staff will know you're with me."<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Arcology Ballroom]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Arcology Ballroom
<<location "arcology_glasshouse">><<effects>>
<<set _partySeen to $xchange.arcology.party.seen>>
<<if !_partySeen.includes("arrived")>>
	<<run _partySeen.push("arrived")>>
	The Glasshouse takes up the entire top of the tower.
	<br><br>
	Through the windows, you can see the city below. Tall buildings stand beneath the city's huge outer dome, with vehicles travelling between them on roads built at different heights.
	<br><br>
	Around two hundred guests have gathered for the party, all wearing masks. Some are dancing to music played by three musicians, while others are drinking and talking near the tables. Many of the guests have perfectly smooth skin or expensive-looking cybernetic implants, which shine under the lights as they move around the room.
	<br><br>
	There are guards here too. One stands beside the lifts, checking guests as they arrive, while another watches the doors used by the staff.
	<br><br>
	"Take a look at the view," Luchifen says, nodding towards the tables by the windows. "I'll be around if you need me."
	<br><br>
	Before you can answer, another guest approaches and touches Luchifen's sleeve to get their attention. Luchifen turns to greet the guest, exchanging a few words before following the guest into the crowd.
<<else>>
	You are standing near the dance floor in the Glasshouse, surrounded by guests enjoying the party. The bar is on the other side of the room, past the dancers, while tables are lined up beside the windows.
	<br><br>
	A line of white lights shows the way back to the lifts, and the three musicians continue playing on a raised platform where they can see over the crowd.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<arcologyicon "dancers">><<link [[Cross to the dancers (0:01)|Arcology Party Floor]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
<br>
<<arcologyicon "raisedbar">><<link [[Raised bar (0:01)|Arcology Party Bar]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
<br>
<<arcologyicon "windows">><<link [[Go to the window tables (0:01)|Arcology Party Windows]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
<br><br>
<<arcologyicon "lift">><<link [[Return to the lift lobby (0:01)|Arcology Party Foyer]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Party Floor
<<location "arcology_glasshouse">><<effects>>
You walk around the edge of the dance floor, carefully moving past the couples dancing nearby. The floor is made of glass, allowing you to see the city far below. Small lights between the glass tiles make it easier to see where you're walking.
<br><br>
On the other side of the room, you spot Luchifen talking with a few guests beside a large pillar. They seem happy to watch everyone dancing without joining in.
<br><br>
<<if !$xchange.arcology.party.seen.includes("fashion")>>
	At the edge of the floor, a guest in a gold mask is turning slowly in front of three friends, showing off a new body.
	<br><br>
	<<socialiseicon "ask">><<link [[Talk to the show-off (0:20)|Arcology Party Fashion]]>><<pass 20>><<arcologyNPC 1 "glass" "guest">><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<socialiseicon>><<link [[Go over to Luchifen (0:01)|Arcology Party Circle]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
<br>
<<if !$xchange.arcology.party.seen.includes("dance")>>
	<<if setup.arcology.reliefLeft("dance")>><<dancestudioicon>><<link [[Dance (0:20)|Arcology Party Dance]]>><<pass 20>><<arcologyNPC 1 "glass" "guest">><<run setup.arcology.relief("dance")>><<stress -4>><</link>><<lstress>><br><</if>>
<</if>>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Step away|Arcology Ballroom]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Party Bar
<<location "arcology_glasshouse">><<effects>>
Three steps lead up to the bar, which is slightly higher than the dance floor. From there, you can see the people dancing and the windows on the other side of the room. Bottles of alcohol are kept in a glass cabinet behind the counter.
<br><br>
The music is loud, so guests have to lean closer to the bartender to be heard. Near the wall, there is a path between two large pillars leading to the staff doors. Further along, you can see a quieter seating area, with palm trees separating it from the rest of the room.
<br><br>
<<if !$xchange.arcology.party.seen.includes("alibi")>>Further along the bar, a group in matching black masks keeps bursting into loud laughter. <</if>><<if !$xchange.arcology.party.seen.includes("ask")>>Near the drinks, a tall guest in a silver mask keeps folding and unfolding a pair of unusually long arms.<</if>>
<br><br>
<<if !$xchange.arcology.party.seen.includes("alibi")>>
	<<icon "mark.gif">><<link [[Listen to the laughter (0:15)|Arcology Party Alibi]]>><<pass 15>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<if !$xchange.arcology.party.seen.includes("ask")>>
	<<socialiseicon "ask">><<link [[Talk to the tall guest (0:15)|Arcology Party Ask]]>><<pass 15>><<arcologyNPC 1 "glass" "guest">><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<icon "prison-run.png">><<link [[Walk between the pillars (0:01)|Arcology Party Gallery]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
<br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Go back down to the ballroom|Arcology Ballroom]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Party Gallery
<<location "arcology_glasshouse">><<effects>>
Past the bar, the music is quieter. Large, comfortable chairs are placed between the pillars, while tall palm plants partly hide several small tables for two people.
<br><br>
A waiter walks between the tables, collecting empty glasses. Nearby, a guard checks the security seal on a staff-only door to make sure nobody has opened it. You also notice a patch of fresh paint beside the door's lock.<<if !$xchange.arcology.party.seen.includes("corner")>> Two guests in matching blue masks walk past you towards the palm trees, talking in low voices.<</if>>
<br>
<<if !$xchange.arcology.party.seen.includes("patron")>>
	<br>
	<<icon "mark.gif">><<link [[Watch a waiter (0:15)|Arcology Party Patron]]>><<pass 15>><<arcologyNPC 1 "vip" "patron">><<arcologyNPC 2 "staff" "waiter">><</link>>
<</if>>
<<if !$xchange.arcology.party.seen.includes("corner")>>
	<br>
	<<icon "mark.gif">><<link [[Follow two guests (0:15)|Arcology Party Corner]]>><<pass 15>><</link>>
<</if>>
<br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Return to the raised bar|Arcology Party Bar]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Party Windows
<<location "arcology_glasshouse">><<effects>>
The tables are arranged beside the curved glass wall of the Glasshouse, with plenty of space between them. You can see people talking at the other tables, but they're too far away to hear unless you walk closer.
<br><br>
Through the glass, you can see large advertising screens on the rooftops below. A flying ambulance moves down between two tall buildings, its warning lights flashing. The guests nearby continue chatting and drinking without paying much attention to it.
<br><br>
Several screens above the tables show information about the private sales taking place tonight. Some guests touch the side of their heads to check the sales through their implants before returning to their drinks.<<if !$xchange.arcology.party.xchanged and !$xchange.arcology.party.seen.includes("stare")>> Across the room, you notice a masked guest staring at you from another table.<</if>><<if !$xchange.arcology.party.seen.includes("vanished")>> At the table nearest the glass, a guest in a plain grey mask sits alone with a glass of water, watching the city instead of the room.<</if>>
<br><br>
<<if !$xchange.arcology.party.seen.includes("vanished")>>
	<<icon "avery-atrium.png">><<link [[Sit with a quiet guest (0:30)|Arcology Party Vanished]]>><<pass 30>><<arcologyNPC 1 "glass" "guest">><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<if !$xchange.arcology.party.xchanged and !$xchange.arcology.party.seen.includes("stare")>>
	<<icon "antique/antique-gold-mask.png">><<link [[Approach the masked guest (0:10)|Arcology Party Stare]]>><<pass 10>><<arcologyNPC 1 "glass" "guest">><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<if !$xchange.arcology.party.seen.includes("displays")>>
	<<arcologyicon "display">><<link [[Read the display (0:10)|Arcology Party Displays]]>><<pass 10>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Walk back to the ballroom|Arcology Ballroom]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Party Circle
<<location "arcology_glasshouse">><<effects>>
Luchifen stands with a small group of guests near a pillar, where they have a clear view of the dance floor. Other guests occasionally stop to greet them on their way from the bar to the tables near the windows.
<br><br>
When you approach, Luchifen moves aside to make room for you. Another guest who was about to join the group notices this and steps back, allowing you to stand beside Luchifen.
<br><br>
<<if !$xchange.arcology.party.seen.includes("luchifen")>>
	<<socialiseicon "ask">><<link [[Join Luchifen (0:20)|Arcology Party Luchifen]]>><<pass 20>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<if !$xchange.arcology.party.seen.includes("close")>>
	<<socialiseicon>><<link [[Stay near Luchifen (0:30)|Arcology Party Close]]>><<pass 30>><<arcologyNPC 1 "vip" "guest">><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Back to the dance floor|Arcology Party Floor]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Party Foyer
<<location "arcology_glasshouse">><<effects>>
You leave the ballroom and enter the lift lobby. A pair of thick glass doors closes behind you, making the music from the party much quieter.
<<if Time.date.timeStamp lt $xchange.arcology.party.at + 4 * 3600>>Some guests are gathering near the windows, waiting for the midnight unmasking.<<else>>Most of the guests have already removed their masks, although the party is still going on.<</if>>
<br><br>
A guard stands beside the lift's access panel, which still shows your guest authorisation. There is another lift nearby, marked for staff use.
<br><br>
<<set _partyTalks to new Set($xchange.arcology.party.seen.filter(t => ["fashion", "vanished", "alibi", "patron", "luchifen", "stare", "close", "ask", "dance", "displays", "corner"].includes(t))).size>>
<<if _partyTalks gte 3 or Time.date.timeStamp gte $xchange.arcology.party.at + 4 * 3600>>
	<<if Time.date.timeStamp lt $xchange.arcology.party.at + 4 * 3600>>You have time for another conversation, or you could stay by the windows until midnight.<<else>>The trio stops playing, and guests begin gathering beneath the screens.<</if>>
	<br>
	<<icon "antiques/antique-watch.gif">><<link [[Midnight|Arcology Party Midnight]]>><<pass `Math.max(0, Math.ceil(($xchange.arcology.party.at + 4 * 3600 - Time.date.timeStamp) / 60))`>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<span class="blue">The guests are waiting for midnight</span>. Talk to a few more people before then.
	<br>
<</if>>
<br>
<<arcologyicon "glasshouse">><<link [[Go back into the ballroom|Arcology Ballroom]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<arcologyicon "street">><<link [[Leave the party|Arcology Party Leave Confirm]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Party Fashion
<<effects>><<run $xchange.arcology.party.seen.push("fashion")>>
<<if !$NPCList[1] or !$NPCList[1].cyber>><<arcologyNPC 1 "glass" "guest">><</if>>
<<person2>>
A <<person>> wearing a gold mask stands with three friends, slowly turning around. The back of <<his>> outfit is open, leaving most of <<his>> back uncovered. <<arcologyCyberLook 1>>
"This is my third body this year. I know, I know. I change too often, but the last one had terrible knees."
<br><br>
<<His>> friends laugh, and one of them steps closer to pinch the skin on <<his>> arm, curious about how soft it feels.
<br><br>
"What about you?" <<he>> asks, looking at your body. "Have you changed bodies too?"
<br><br>
<<if $xchange.arcology.party.xchanged>>
	You look down at yourself, wondering how <<he>> guessed.
	<br><br>
	"Still getting used to your new body?" <<he>> asks. "I had one with longer arms before. I kept reaching too far whenever I tried to pick something up, and it took me a whole week to get used to them."
<<else>>
	You tell <<him>> that you arrived at the party in the body you were born in.
	<br><br>
	"How brave. Or how poor." <<His>> friends laugh, and <<he>> gives your arm a friendly pat. "I'm joking!"
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Party Floor]]>><<clearsinglenpc 1>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Party Vanished
<<effects>><<run $xchange.arcology.party.seen.push("vanished")>>
<<if !$NPCList[1] or !$NPCList[1].cyber>><<arcologyNPC 1 "glass" "guest">><</if>>
<<person2>>
By the window, a <<person>> wearing a plain grey mask sits alone with a glass of water. <<arcologyCyberLook 1>> When you approach the table, <<he>> moves <<his>> chair aside to make room for you.
<br><br>
"First time here?" <<he>> asks. You nod. "I came here four years ago. Before that, I was a nurse in a city a long way from here."
<br><br>
<<He>> looks out of the window for a while, watching the lights outside. You are about to ask another question when <<he>> starts talking again.
"Someone used to follow me everywhere. Whenever I moved to a new flat or got another job, the same face was waiting for me. I went to the police so many times that they had a huge pile of reports about it."
<br><br>
"I'm probably still being looked for," <<he>> continues. "But only for my old face. I came to this island with a new face and a new handle. Nobody here has ever asked me for my real name."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Party Vanished 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Party Vanished 2
<<effects>><<person2>>
"Do you miss your old life?" you ask.
<br><br>
<<He>> looks down at <<his>> glass, taking some time to think before answering. "I miss hearing my mother's voice on the phone. That's about it."
<br><br>
<<He>> drinks the rest of <<his>> water and puts the empty glass on the table.
<br><br>
"People here talk about money all the time," <<he>> says. "But some of us came here because we needed somewhere safe. This is the first place I've lived where I don't have to worry about someone finding me."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Party Windows]]>><<clearsinglenpc 1>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Party Alibi
<<effects>><<run $xchange.arcology.party.seen.push("alibi")>>
At the bar, a group of guests in matching black masks are laughing so loudly that the bartender has stopped pretending not to hear.
<br><br>
"So the judge asks where the defendant is," one of them says, "and the lawyer stands up and says, honestly, that the client no longer exists." More laughter. "Case dismissed. Three years of evidence, and no body to put it on!"
<br><br>
The storyteller has very smooth hands and a very young face. One of the friends lifts a glass. "To absent friends."
<br><br>
"To absent friends," the others say, and they all look at the storyteller and laugh again.
<br><br>
The bartender looks directly at you for a second before returning to polishing a glass that is already clean.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Party Bar]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Party Patron
<<effects>>
<<run $xchange.arcology.party.seen.push("patron")>>
<<if !$NPCList[1] or !$NPCList[1].cyber>><<arcologyNPC 1 "vip" "patron">><<arcologyNPC 2 "staff" "waiter">><</if>>
<<person2>>Near the pillars, an elderly <<person>> in a jewelled mask has stopped a waiter. <<arcologyCyberLook 1>>
<<person3>>The waiter is a nervous young <<personsimple>> holding a tray too tightly.
<br><br>
<<person2>>"I've watched you all night," the patron says. "You're too good for this. A new face, your debts cleared, a room on the upper terraces. All you'd have to do is sign with my house for a year."
<br><br>
<<He>> takes a pill from a breast pocket and puts it on the waiter's tray beside the glasses. "Think how different your life would be. Think how different you would be."
<br><br>
<<person3>>The waiter looks at the pill and doesn't pick it up. <<He>> doesn't walk away either.
<br><br>
<<link [[Step in|Arcology Party Patron 2]]>><<set $phase to "step">><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Leave it|Arcology Party Patron 2]]>><<set $phase to "leave">><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Threaten the patron|Arcology Party Patron 2]]>><<set $phase to "threat">><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Party Patron 2
<<effects>>
<<if $phase is "threat">>
	<<set $xchange.arcology.party.stepIn to true>>
	<<if !$xchange.arcology.trouble>><<set $xchange.arcology.trouble to { source: "patron" }>><</if>>
	<<run setup.arcology.partySlip("blunder")>>
	<<person2>>You move between the patron and the waiter. "Leave the waiter alone," you say. "Bother anyone again and everyone here will hear about it." The patron looks down at your hands, then at <<if $worn.face.name is "white half-mask">>the white mask covering your face<<else>>the white mask you're carrying<</if>>.
	<br><br>
	"You should ask your sponsor how long the mask protects you." <<He>> takes the pill off the tray and walks away. Near the lift, <<he>> stops to speak to two people in plain coats, pointing you out with <<his>> glass.
	<br><br>
	<<person3>>The waiter grips your sleeve. "Please don't go outside alone," <<he>> says, before someone calls <<him>> back to work.
<<elseif $phase is "step">>
	<<set $xchange.arcology.party.stepIn to true>>
	<<person2>>You walk up, take a glass off the tray, and ask the waiter loudly where the bathrooms are. The patron turns to tell you to go away. Then <<he>> notices your white mask and glances towards Luchifen, who is watching from across the room. <<He>> closes <<his>> mouth.
	<br><br>
	"Another time," <<he>> says to the waiter, and takes the pill back. <<He>> goes off into the crowd without looking at you again.
	<br><br>
	<<person3>>The waiter breathes out. "Thanks," <<he>> says quietly. "There'll be another offer tomorrow, though... Kind of normal here."
<<else>>
	You look away. When you look back a few minutes later, the tray is on a side table, and the waiter is following the patron towards a private lift at the back of the room. The pill is gone.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<if $phase is "leave">>
	<<set $skulduggerydifficulty to 700>>
	<<link [[Follow them (0:10)|Arcology Party Patron Follow]]>><<pass 10>><</link>><<skulduggerydifficulty>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<link [[Return to the gallery|Arcology Party Gallery]]>><<clearsinglenpc 1>><<clearsinglenpc 2>><<set $phase to 0>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Party Patron Follow
<<effects>>
<<run setup.arcology.partySlip("nosy")>>
<<set $skulduggerydifficulty to 700>><<skulduggerycheck "silent">>
You keep a few guests between you and the patron, who leads the waiter along the back wall.
<br><br>
<<if $skulduggerysuccess is 1>>
	The private lift is behind a curtain of falling water lit from beneath. The patron says something to the guard in white beside it, and the guard looks at the floor while they step inside.
	Through the glass you watch the numbers count down past every lit floor and stop at one that has no number, only a black square.
	<br><br>
	When the lift comes back up, it is empty, and the waiter's tray is still on the side table.
	<br><br>
	<span class="green">Nobody noticed you following.</span>
	<<run $xchange.arcology.party.seen.pushUnique("lift")>>
<<else>>
	You are halfway along the wall when a guard in a white suit steps into your path.
	<br><br>
	"Private lift, guest," the guard says, and doesn't move until you turn around. By the time you look again, the patron and the waiter are gone.
	<br><br>
	<span class="red">You were noticed.</span> <<stress 3>><<gstress>><<run setup.arcology.expose()>>
	<<run setup.arcology.partySlip("blunder")>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<arcologyPartyBack "Arcology Party Gallery" "Next">>

:: Arcology Party Stare
<<effects>>
<<run $xchange.arcology.party.seen.push("stare")>>
<<if !$NPCList[1] or !$NPCList[1].cyber>><<arcologyNPC 1 "glass" "guest">><</if>>
<<person2>>
The masked <<person>> watches you as you approach. <<arcologyCyberLook 1>> When you reach <<him>>, <<he>> offers you <<his>> hand, and you shake it.
<br><br>
"Excuse me," <<he>> says. "You look familiar. Have we met somewhere on the mainland?"
<br><br>
"I don't think so," you say. "Maybe I just look like someone you know."
<br><br>
"Perhaps," <<he>> replies with a smile.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Party Stare 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Party Stare 2
<<effects>><<person2>>
After you finish talking, you say goodbye and walk away.
<br><br>
When you look back, you notice <<him>> typing something on the small screen on <<his>> wrist.
<br><br>
You came to the island using your real body, and <span class="purple">someone may have recognised you.</span>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Party Windows]]>><<clearsinglenpc 1>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Party Luchifen
<<effects>><<run $xchange.arcology.party.seen.push("luchifen")>>
You stand beside Luchifen, listening as several guests try to tell the same story. They keep interrupting each other, with one guest adding a name someone forgot and another correcting how much money was involved.
Luchifen laughs at the correction, making the guest who said it smile proudly.
<br><br>
A large guest wearing a red mask approaches the group and starts to speak, then notices Luchifen and stops halfway through the sentence. The guest quickly apologises and walks away, leaving the others to continue talking.
<br><br>
While the conversation continues, another guest steps closer and touches Luchifen's elbow to get their attention. The guest quietly puts something into Luchifen's hand. It looks like a small data chip, but Luchifen simply puts it in their pocket without looking at it or speaking to the guest.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Party Luchifen 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Party Luchifen 2
<<effects>>
As the others begin arguing about the story again, Luchifen turns towards you with a smile.
"Enjoying yourself?"
<br><br>
"Who are all these people to you?" you ask quietly.
<br><br>
"Guests, just like you."
They smile and <<if $worn.face.name is "white half-mask">>reach over to adjust the ribbon on your mask, even though it is already tied properly<<else>>take the loose ribbon of the mask you're carrying and smooth it between their fingers, though there is no knot in it<</if>>. Before you can ask anything else, someone nearby calls their name.
<br><br>
Luchifen looks towards the person calling them, then turns back to you. "Excuse me a moment," they say, turning to greet the newcomer while you remain with the group.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Party Circle]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Party Close
<<effects>>
<<run $xchange.arcology.party.seen.push("close")>>
<<if !$NPCList[1] or !$NPCList[1].cyber>><<arcologyNPC 1 "vip" "guest">><</if>>
<<person2>>
You stay close to Luchifen as they introduce you to the other guests. They only use your handle when introducing you, and nobody asks for your real name.
<br><br>
A <<person>> comes over to greet you and takes your hand. <<He>> speaks in a calm, confident voice, but keeps holding your hand longer than you expected.
<br><br>
<<arcologyCyberLook 1>> "So, how did you meet Luchifen?"
<br><br>
<<link [[Tell the truth|Arcology Party Close 2]]>><<set $phase to "truth">><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Smile and say nothing|Arcology Party Close 2]]>><<set $phase to "quiet">><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Party Close 2
<<effects>><<person2>>
<<if $phase is "truth">>
	You start to talk about the town—
	<br><br>
	"At the docks," Luchifen answers for you. "You should try getting out more."
	<br><br>
	The <<person>> laughs and lets go of your hand. Luchifen leads you away from the group towards the windows, where the other guests are too far away to hear your conversation.
	<br><br>
	"That one likes asking people where they live," Luchifen explains quietly. "Then <<he>> looks up information about them later. Be careful what you tell anyone, especially your address."
	<br><br>
	They wait by the windows until the guest has joined another conversation, then lead you back towards the pillar and the people gathered around it.
<<else>>
	You smile but say nothing. The <<person>> waits for you to answer, then laughs and lets go of your hand.
	<br><br>
	"Oh, I like <<phim>>," <<he>> says to Luchifen. "Where did you meet <<phim>>?"
	<br><br>
	"Here and there," Luchifen replies with a smile, giving <<him>> no further explanation.
	<br><br>
	After the guest walks away, Luchifen moves closer and lowers their voice so nobody else can hear.
	<br><br>
	"If you'd started answering <<his>> questions, <<he>> would have kept you talking all evening," they say. "It's better to let <<him>> wonder."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Party Circle]]>><<clearsinglenpc 1>><<set $phase to 0>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Party Ask
<<effects>>
<<run $xchange.arcology.party.seen.push("ask")>>
<<if !$NPCList[1] or !$NPCList[1].cyber>><<arcologyNPC 1 "glass" "guest">><</if>>
<<person2>>
A tall <<person>> wearing a silver mask stands near the drinks, holding a glass in one hand. <<His>> arms are unusually long and pale.
<br><br>
<<He>> tries resting <<his>> free arm at <<his>> side, then folds it across <<his>> chest, still looking uncomfortable with the position. <<arcologyCyberLook 1>>
<br><br>
<<if $xchange.arcology.party.xchanged>>
	<<He>> notices you watching and smiles. "New body too?" <<he>> asks. "Took me nearly a month to get used to these arms. I kept forgetting how long they were."
<<else>>
	<<He>> notices you looking at <<him>> and lifts one long arm with a rueful smile. "New body. I still haven't worked out what to do with these."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Ask more about it|Arcology Party Ask 2]]>><<set $phase to "gentle">><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Ask about the life before|Arcology Party Ask 2]]>><<set $phase to "pushy">><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Party Ask 2
<<effects>><<person2>>
<<if $phase is "gentle">>
	"Sometimes I see myself in a mirror and think I'm looking at a stranger," <<he>> says with a laugh. "I'm getting used to this face, though. I like it much better than my last one."
	<<if $xchange.arcology.party.xchanged>>
		<br><br>
		"Maybe you'll feel the same about yours after a while," <<he>> adds. "If you still don't like it, you can always buy another one."
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	<<run $xchange.arcology.party.seen.push("nosy")>>
	<<run setup.arcology.partySlip("nosy")>>
	<<He>> keeps smiling, but <<he>> grips the glass more firmly. "Who did you come with?"
	<br><br>
	You tell <<him>>, and <<he>> looks across the room at Luchifen before putting <<his>> glass down.
	<br><br>
	"Then ask Luchifen about it," <<he>> says.
<</if>>
<br>
<<if $phase is "pushy">>
	<br>
	<<link [[Keep asking|Arcology Party Ask Insist]]>><<arcologyNPC 2 "under" "guest">><</link>>
<</if>>
<<set $phase to 0>>
