:: Arcology Party Dance
<<effects>>
<<run $xchange.arcology.party.seen.push("dance")>>
<<if !$NPCList[1] or !$NPCList[1].cyber>><<arcologyNPC 1 "glass" "guest">><</if>>
<<person2>>
As the three musicians begin playing a waltz, a <<person>> wearing a white feather mask approaches you and offers <<his>> hand. You accept, and <<he>> leads you onto the dance floor. <<arcologyCyberLook 1>>
<br><br>
<<He>> starts dancing slowly, giving you time to get used to the steps. When another couple comes too close, <<he>> gently guides you around them so you can continue dancing without bumping into anyone.
<br><br>
As you become more comfortable, the two of you start talking about the music. <<He>> listens to what you have to say, occasionally smiling or adding a comment of <<his>> own.
<br><br>
Neither of you asks for the other's name, and you continue dancing together until the music ends.<<danceskill 3>><<gdanceskill>>
<br><br>
<<He>> lets go of your hand and gives you a small bow. "Thank you, stranger," <<he>> says with a smile before walking away and disappearing into the crowd.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Party Floor]]>><<clearsinglenpc 1>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Party Displays
<<effects>>
<<run $xchange.arcology.party.seen.push("displays")>>
Several large screens are attached near the top of the dome, arranged in a circle. Most of them show different parts of the city below, but one displays a list of things being offered for sale.
<br><br>
<<holo "GLASSHOUSE / PRIVATE LOTS" "pending">>
	<<holoRow "LOT 11" "CLEAN IDENTITY, NO PRIOR RECORD. CLOSED">>
	<<holoRow "LOT 12" "MEDICAL HISTORY, ERASED. CLOSED">>
	<<holoRow "LOT 13" "[WITHHELD]">>
	<<holoLine "BIDDING RESTRICTED TO VERIFIED MEMBERS" "denied">>
<</holo>>
<br>
Nobody near you is looking at it. The guest beside you finishes a drink and taps a wrist screen, and one of the closed lots changes colour.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Party Windows]]>><</link>>
