:: Arcology Party Corner 2
<<effects>>
<<run $xchange.arcology.party.seen.push("corner")>>
<<if $phase is "listen">>
	<<run setup.arcology.partySlip("nosy")>>
	<<set $skulduggerydifficulty to 500>><<skulduggerycheck "silent">>
	You walk behind a group of palm trees and stop where the guests can't easily see you. You're still close enough to hear their conversation, so you turn towards the bar and pretend to be waiting for someone.
	<br><br>
	"...not until the list is signed," one of the guests says. "And nobody's signing it until Luchifen has checked it."
	<br><br>
	"Then we'd better make sure Luchifen approves."
	<br><br>
	<<if $skulduggerysuccess is 1>>
		"You can't make Luchifen approve anything," the other guest replies. "They decide who gets lot thirteen. The rest of us can only bid on what's left."
		<br><br>
		You hear them tap their glasses together before the conversation continues.
		"Someone's paying a lot of money for that one. A completely new face for someone the mainland police are still looking for. I don't know who the buyer is, but the buyer must be desperate to hide."
		<br><br>
		You decide you've heard enough and quietly walk away from the palm trees while the guests continue talking.
		<br><br>
		<span class="green">You leave without being noticed.</span>
		<<run $xchange.arcology.party.seen.pushUnique("lot13")>>
	<<else>>
		"You can't make Luchifen approve anything," the other guest replies. There's a short pause. "Wait. Is someone listening?"
		<br><br>
		<<if !$NPCList[1] or !$NPCList[1].cyber>><<arcologyNPC 1 "glass" "guest">><</if>><<person2>>
		Before you can walk away, a <<person>> wearing a blue mask comes around the palm trees and finds you standing there. <<arcologyCyberLook 1>>
		<br><br>
		<<He>> notices your white mask and looks at you more closely.
		"You're Luchifen's guest... Then I'm sure you understand that you haven't heard anything important."
		<br><br>
		<<He>> steps aside to let you leave, although <<he>> continues watching until you've walked away.
		<br><br>
		<span class="red">You were caught listening.</span> <<stress 3>><<gstress>><<run setup.arcology.expose()>>
		<<run setup.arcology.partySlip("blunder")>>
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	You decide to leave the guests to their conversation and walk away. Whatever they're discussing, you don't want to risk being caught listening.
<</if>>
<<set $phase to 0>>
<br><br>
<<arcologyPartyBack "Arcology Party Gallery" "Next">>
<br>

:: Arcology Party Bothered
<<location "arcology_glasshouse">><<effects>>
<<run $xchange.arcology.party.seen.pushUnique("bothered")>>
<<if !$NPCList[1] or !$NPCList[1].cyber>><<arcologyNPC 1 "vip" "guest">><</if>>
<<person2>>
As you walk back through the Glasshouse, you pass a group of guests talking near the pillars. They stop talking when they notice you, only continuing once you've walked past. One of them still watches you as you leave. At a nearby table, another guest quickly turns a small card face down when you approach, hiding whatever is written on it.
<br><br>
A <<person>> wearing a gold mask walks towards you and stops in front of you. <<arcologyCyberLook 1>> <<He>> gives you a polite smile.
<br><br>
"You've been asking a lot of questions tonight," <<he>> says. "Several guests have mentioned it to me. Some of them came here because they want to keep their identities private, and they don't appreciate being questioned."
<br><br>
<<link [[Apologise|Arcology Party Bothered 2]]>><<set $phase to "sorry">><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Ask who complained|Arcology Party Bothered 2]]>><<set $phase to "ask">><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Say it's nobody else's business|Arcology Party Bothered 2]]>><<set $phase to "rude">><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Party Bothered 2
<<location "arcology_glasshouse">><<effects>><<person2>><<speechresolve>>
<<switch $phase>>
<<case "sorry">>
	<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
		<<case "meek">>
			"Sorry. I didn't know I was upsetting anyone," you say.
		<<case "shy">>
			You glance towards the other guests. "I'm sorry. I didn't mean to upset them."
		<<case "polite">>
			You sigh. "I'm sorry. I should have been more careful about what I asked."
		<<case "confident">>
			You sigh. "I'm sorry I bothered them. It won't happen again."
		<<case "bratty">>
			You sigh. "All right, sorry. I didn't know everyone was so touchy about questions."
		<<case "docile">>
			"I'm sorry. I'll leave them alone," you say.
		<<case "flamboyant">>
			You sigh. "My apologies. I didn't mean to spoil anyone's evening."
		<<case "cruel">>
			You sigh. "Sorry. I won't waste their time with more questions."
		<<default>>
			You sigh. "Sorry. I'm new here."
	<</switch>>
	<br><br>
	The <<person>> gives a small nod. "Then you've learned something useful tonight," <<he>> says, stepping aside to let you pass.
	<<stress 2>><<gstress>>
<<case "rude">>
	<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
		<<case "meek">>
			"I don't think it's anyone else's business what I ask," you say, trying to keep your voice steady.
		<<case "shy">>
			You say, "But... why are they talking about me? It isn't their business."
		<<case "polite">>
			You say, "With respect, what I ask someone is between me and that person."
		<<case "confident">>
			You say, "They can speak to me themselves. My questions aren't their business."
		<<case "bratty">>
			You say, "Tell them to mind their own business."
		<<case "docile">>
			You say, "I'd rather they didn't talk about me. It's my business who I speak to."
		<<case "flamboyant">>
			You say, "Surely they have more interesting things to discuss than my questions."
		<<case "cruel">>
			You say, "They can mind their own business. I don't care what they think."
		<<default>>
			You say, "What I ask people is nobody else's business."
	<</switch>>
	<br><br>
	The <<person>> keeps smiling. "Of course. Enjoy the rest of your evening." <<He>> turns away and speaks into the screen on <<his>> wrist. Across the room, a guest in a black mask starts watching you.
	<<run setup.arcology.partySlip("blunder")>>
<<default>>
	<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
		<<case "meek">>
			"Could you tell me who complained?" you ask.
		<<case "shy">>
			"Who was it?" you ask. "Who complained about me?"
		<<case "polite">>
			You say, "May I ask who brought this to your attention?"
		<<case "confident">>
			You say, "I'd like to know who complained. Can you tell me?"
		<<case "bratty">>
			You say, "Who's been complaining about me behind my back?"
		<<case "docile">>
			You say, "Would you tell me who it was? I just want to know."
		<<case "flamboyant">>
			You say, "At least tell me who's been talking about me."
		<<case "cruel">>
			You say, "Who complained? I'd like to know who's been spreading my name around."
		<<default>>
			You say, "Who complained about me?"
	<</switch>>
	<br><br>
	The <<person>> laughs softly. "You really can't stop asking questions, can you?" <<He>> walks away without answering. A minute later, a guest you've never spoken to passes close enough to warn you to mind your own business before someone makes you leave.
	<<run setup.arcology.partySlip("blunder")>>
<</switch>>
<br><br>
<<set _bothBack to $xchange.arcology.party.back or "Arcology Ballroom">>
<<link [[Next|_bothBack]]>><<clearsinglenpc 1>><<set $phase to 0>><<unset $xchange.arcology.party.back>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Party Ambush
<<location "arcology">><<effects>>
<<if !$NPCList[1] or !$NPCList[1].cyber>><<arcologyNPC 1 "vip" "merchant">><</if>>
<<person2>>
The lift opens at the bottom of the tower. You step outside onto the quiet street, but before you can get far, someone grabs your arm from behind. <<He>> turns you around and pushes you against the glass wall beside the entrance, hurting your shoulder.<<gpain>>
<br><br>
It is a <<person>> you saw upstairs, mask gone now. <<His>> other hand has opened into a set of thin metal blades. "You looked at things that aren't yours, and I sell implants. I can take one back out just as easily."
<br><br>
You turn your head and see Luchifen standing inside the lobby, on the other side of the glass. They are watching what is happening, but make no move to help you.
<<pain 4>><<stress 6>><<gstress>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Struggle|Arcology Party Ambush 2]]>><<set $phase to "struggle">><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Keep still|Arcology Party Ambush 2]]>><<set $phase to "still">><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Party Ambush 2
<<location "arcology">><<effects>><<person2>>
<<if $phase is "struggle">>
	You try to pull away, but the merchant keeps a firm grip on you. As you twist your body, the blades scrape against the glass beside your face. You raise your arm to protect yourself, only for one of them to cut across it. <<pain 8>><<ggpain>>
<<else>>
	You stay still as the merchant slowly brings the blades towards the small light behind your ear. <<His>> hand is already close to your face, leaving you little room to move without touching one of the blades.
<</if>>
<br><br>
A figure in a dark coat steps out from beside the doors, takes the merchant's wrist, and turns it. The merchant goes down onto the pavement face first, with a knee in <<his>> back and <<his>> bladed hand pinned flat against the stone.
<br><br>
It takes about a second.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Party Ambush 3]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Party Ambush 3
<<effects>><<set _umbrellaKnown to setup.arcology.umbrellaKnown()>><<person2>><<arcologyVictorPronouns>>
<<if _umbrellaKnown>>
	You recognise the dark coat. It is the tall, quiet <<print _vman>> who held the umbrella over Luchifen at the docks. <<print _vHe>> doesn't look at you any more now than <<print _vhe>> did then.
<<else>>
	<<set $xchange.arcology.umbrella to true>>
	You have never seen this <<print _vman>> before. <<print _vHe>> is tall and quiet, and on the collar of <<print _vhis>> dark coat is a small silver pin shaped like a half mask, the same shape as the mask Luchifen wore tonight. One of Luchifen's people, you think.
<</if>>
<br><br>
The merchant starts protesting, although it's difficult to understand <<him>> with <<his>> face pressed against the pavement. You manage to hear something about a misunderstanding, but the <<print _vman>> in the dark coat ignores <<him>>.
<br><br>
The lobby doors open again, and Luchifen walks outside without rushing. They stop beside the merchant and look down at <<him>>, then turn towards you.
<br><br>
"You made quite a lot of noise tonight. I was curious to see who would come looking for you." They turn towards the <<print _vman>> holding the merchant down. "Take that somewhere quiet."
<br><br>
The <<print _vman>> pulls the merchant up from the pavement while Luchifen turns back to you.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Party Ambush 4]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Party Ambush 4
<<effects>>
"You're my guest," Luchifen says. "Nobody is allowed to hurt my guests, and by tomorrow morning, everyone on this street will know that."
<br><br>
<<if $phase is "struggle">>
	They notice the cut on your arm and take a closer look at where the blade struck you.
<<else>>
	They look behind your ear, checking the small light the merchant was trying to reach.
<</if>>
<br><br>
"Of course, that protection only lasts while you're my guest," they continue. "Remember that. If you attract this much trouble again, I might not be nearby to help you."
<<unset $xchange.arcology.trouble>><<set $phase to 0>>
<br><br>
<<arcologyicon "hotel">><<link [[Go back to the hotel (0:05)|Arcology Hotel Room]]>><<pass 5>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Party Leave Confirm
<<effects>>
You head for the door. The guard in the white suit looks at you, then over your shoulder, where Luchifen is somewhere in the crowd.
<br><br>
If you leave now, <span class="red">you'll walk out on Luchifen's party.</span>
<br><br>
<<link [[Leave|Arcology Party Failed]]>><<set $xchange.arcology.party.why to "left">><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Stay|Arcology Party Foyer]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Party Midnight
<<effects>>
You go back through the glass doors and follow the small lights on the floor towards the tables by the windows.
<br><br>
<<if Time.date.timeStamp lte $xchange.arcology.party.at + 4 * 3600>>
	At midnight, the bright lights above the party slowly turn off, making it easier to see the city through the windows. Someone begins counting down from ten, and the guests start turning towards one another. When the count reaches one, everyone takes off their masks.
	<br><br>
	<<if $worn.face.name is "white half-mask">>You remove yours as well, watching the guests laugh and talk as they show their faces to one another.<<faceundress "wardrobe">><<else>>You keep the unused white mask in your hand, watching the guests laugh and talk as they show their faces to one another.<</if>>
<<else>>
	The lights above the party have already been turned down, and you can see the city through the windows. Most of the guests have removed their masks and are now talking amongst themselves.
	<<if $worn.face.name is "white half-mask">>You take yours off as well, looking around while the waiters collect empty glasses from the nearby tables.<<faceundress "wardrobe">><<else>>You keep the unused white mask in your hand while the waiters collect empty glasses from the nearby tables.<</if>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
You look around at the faces of nearly two hundred guests, but you don't recognise anyone. Even with their masks off, you have no way of knowing who these people really are. Some might have changed their bodies, while others might simply be using different names. You realise that taking off a mask doesn't mean much in a place like this.
<br><br>
When you turn to look beside you, Luchifen is already standing there. You didn't notice them coming over. They've taken off their mask too, but their face looks exactly the same as when you first met them. You still don't know whether that's their original face.
<br><br>
"Come outside," they say. "I want to hear what you thought."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Party Talk]]>><<pass 10>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Party Talk
<<effects>>
<<set _pt to $xchange.arcology.party>><<set _pt.asked to _pt.asked or []>>
<<if _pt.asked.length is 0 and !$phase>>
	The balcony goes around the outside of the dome. You step through the glass door, leaving the warm ballroom behind. The air outside is much colder, and the music becomes quieter when the door closes.
	<br><br>
	Luchifen is leaning against the railing, looking down at the city below. They turn towards you as you approach, smiling.
	"You've looked like you wanted to ask me something. Well? What would you like to know?"
<</if>>
<<switch $phase>>
<<case "bodies">>
	You ask Luchifen how people here can change their bodies so often. You know about X-Change, but you thought a person was more or less stuck with one body, not swapping it every time they got bored.
	<br><br>
	Luchifen smiles at your question. They lean against the railing while they think about their answer.
	"You could learn a great deal more about that here, if you wanted. But yes, what you know is the basic idea of it."
	<<if playerIsXChanged()>>
		<br><br>
		They look you over with an amused smile. "Although you already know a little about that, don't you? You're using another body yourself."
	<</if>>
<<case "bodiesKnow">>
	You tell them you already understand how X-Change works. You can choose another body and keep using it, provided you're careful. What surprises you is how easily people here seem to drop one body and take another.
	<br><br>
	Luchifen listens without interrupting. When you finish, they give you a small nod, but don't explain anything further.
<<case "look">>
	You ask why so many people in the city have metal parts on their bodies, artificial eyes, or skin that looks unusually smooth.
	<br><br>
	"Such a wonder, isn't it?" Luchifen says, looking through the glass at the people dancing inside.
	"There are all sorts of ways to change yourself here. You might even get the chance to try some of them."
	<br><br>
	They turn back towards you, still smiling.
	<br><br>
	"Of course, some people end up corrupted by those changes! You'll have to be careful about what you choose."
<<case "stay">>
	You ask why Luchifen still looks the same. You've seen so many people at the party remove their masks and show completely different faces underneath, but Luchifen hasn't changed their appearance at all.
	<br><br>
	"I could ask you the same question," Luchifen replies, looking at you with an amused smile. "Why haven't you changed yours?"
<<case "stayNeed">>
	You tell them you don't see any reason to change your body.
<<case "stayFeel">>
	You tell them you simply don't feel like changing your appearance.
<<case "stayHow">>
	You admit that you'd actually like to change your body, but you have no idea how to get started.
<<case "honest">>
	"Then you must be the most honest person here," you say. "Everyone else keeps changing who they are, but you've stayed the same."
	<br><br>
	Luchifen looks surprised by your answer. Then, they burst out laughing, loudly enough that a couple standing further along the balcony turn to look.
	<br><br>
	"Oh, dear! You really think that?! I'm probably the biggest faker in this whole city!" They laugh again, clearly enjoying your reaction.
	<<npcincr Luchifen love 1>><<glove>>
<<case "who">>
	You ask Luchifen who they really are. Almost everyone at the party seems to know them, and you get the feeling they must be someone important.
	<br><br>
	Luchifen smiles at your question.
	<br><br>
	"Who am I?" they repeat, looking back at the city below. "That's a rather interesting question, isn't it? I wonder that myself. Who am I?"
<</switch>>
<<if ($phase is "stayNeed" or $phase is "stayFeel" or $phase is "stayHow")>>
	<br><br>
	Luchifen listens to your answer, resting their chin on one hand. When you finish, they straighten up and brush some hair away from their face.
	<br><br>
	"Ah, I see. Well, as for me..." They smile and gesture towards themselves. "I'm too beautiful to be changed by anything. Isn't that right?"
<</if>>
<<set _ptLast to $phase>><<set $phase to 0>>
<br><br>
<<if _ptLast is "bodies" and playerIsXChanged()>>
	<<link [[Not this freely|Arcology Party Talk]]>><<set $phase to "bodiesKnow">><</link>>
	<br>
<<elseif _ptLast is "stay">>
	<<link [[No need to|Arcology Party Talk]]>><<set $phase to "stayNeed">><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Don't feel like it|Arcology Party Talk]]>><<set $phase to "stayFeel">><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[I would, but how?|Arcology Party Talk]]>><<set $phase to "stayHow">><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<<set _ptLeft to ["bodies", "look", "stay", "honest", "who"].filter(q => !_pt.asked.includes(q))>>
	<<if _ptLeft.includes("bodies")>>
		<<link [[Ask about changing bodies|Arcology Party Talk]]>><<set $phase to "bodies">><<run _pt.asked.push("bodies")>><</link>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
	<<if _ptLeft.includes("look")>>
		<<link [[Ask why people look like that|Arcology Party Talk]]>><<set $phase to "look">><<run _pt.asked.push("look")>><</link>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
	<<if _ptLeft.includes("stay")>>
		<<link [[Ask why they never change|Arcology Party Talk]]>><<set $phase to "stay">><<run _pt.asked.push("stay")>><</link>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
	<<if _ptLeft.includes("honest") and !_ptLeft.includes("stay")>>
		<<link [[You're the most honest one here|Arcology Party Talk]]>><<set $phase to "honest">><<run _pt.asked.push("honest")>><</link>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
	<<if _ptLeft.includes("who")>>
		<<link [[Ask who they are|Arcology Party Talk]]>><<set $phase to "who">><<run _pt.asked.push("who")>><</link>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
	<<if _ptLeft.length is 0>>
		Luchifen leans back on the railing. "My turn. What did you think of the other guests?"
		<br><br>
		<<link [[They frightened you|Arcology Party End]]>><<set $phase to "afraid">><<run delete _pt.asked>><</link>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Some of them looked free|Arcology Party End]]>><<set $phase to "free">><<run delete _pt.asked>><</link>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Everyone is hiding something|Arcology Party End]]>><<set $phase to "hiding">><<run delete _pt.asked>><</link>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
<</if>>

:: Arcology Party End
<<effects>>
<<if $xchange.arcology.party.status is "done">>
	The party has finished. Most of the guests have gone home, and the staff are busy clearing glasses and plates from the tables inside.
	<br><br>
	Luchifen is no longer on the balcony.
<<else>>
	<<speechresolve>>
	<<switch $phase>>
		<<case "afraid">>
			<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
				<<case "meek">>
					"Some of the guests frightened me," you admit. "I didn't like the way they were looking at people."
				<<case "shy">>
					"Some of them scared me," you say quietly. "I didn't want to stay near them."
				<<case "polite">>
					You say, "I enjoyed the party, but I have to admit that some of the guests frightened me."
				<<case "confident">>
					You say, "Some of those guests frightened me. I'm staying away from them."
				<<case "bratty">>
					You say, "Some of those creeps scared me. Why would you invite people like that?"
				<<case "docile">>
					You say, "I'm glad you invited me, but some of those people really scared me."
				<<case "flamboyant">>
					You say, "The party was interesting, but I must admit that some of the guests frightened me."
				<<case "cruel">>
					You say, "Some of those people scared me. I wouldn't trust any of those bastards."
				<<default>>
					You say, "Some of those people scared me. I didn't feel safe around them."
			<</switch>>
			<br><br>
			"Which ones?" Luchifen asks.
			<br><br>
			You point towards one of the tables through the glass doors. Luchifen turns to look at the guests you mean, then gives a small nod.
			<br><br>
			"Ah, that table. Yes, I'd stay away from them too." They move a little to one side, making room for you beside the railing.
			"If anyone bothers you, tell me. I invited you here, after all. You shouldn't have to deal with them on your own."
		<<case "free">>
			<<if $xchange.arcology.party.seen.includes("vanished")>>
				You remember the guest by the window, who told you that the island was the first place that had ever felt safe.
			<<else>>
				You think about the guests who spoke openly about leaving their old lives behind and starting again here.
			<</if>>
			<br><br>
			<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
				<<case "meek">>
					"I think some of them really are free here," you say. "They couldn't live like this back home."
				<<case "shy">>
					"They seemed happier here," you say. "Some of them, anyway. I think they needed somewhere like this."
				<<case "polite">>
					You say, "I can understand why some of the guests decided to start a new life here."
				<<case "confident">>
					You say, "For some of those people, coming here was probably the best decision they ever made."
				<<case "bratty">>
					You say, "At least some of them can do whatever they want here. Better than having people chase them around back home."
				<<case "docile">>
					You say, "Some of them seem much happier with their new lives. I hope things stay that way for them."
				<<case "flamboyant">>
					You say, "It's nice seeing some of them so happy with the lives they've chosen."
				<<case "cruel">>
					You say, "Some of them escaped from people who wanted to control their lives. Good for them."
				<<default>>
					You say, "Some of them seem happy here. They can finally live the way they want."
			<</switch>>
			<br><br>
			Luchifen looks back through the glass at the party. "If someone from your old life won't leave you alone, having a different face can make it much harder for them to find you.
			Of course, that doesn't mean everyone here is a good person. You've met a few of them tonight. I'm sure you can understand that."
		<<case "hiding">>
			<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
				<<case "meek">>
					"I think everyone in there is hiding something," you say. "Maybe you are too."
				<<case "shy">>
					"I think everyone here has secrets," you say quietly. "Even you, probably."
				<<case "polite">>
					You say, "It seems everyone here has something to hide. I imagine you have your own secrets too."
				<<case "confident">>
					You say, "Everyone here has secrets, including you. I'm sure there's plenty you haven't told me."
				<<case "bratty">>
					You say, "Don't pretend you're any different. I bet you've got more secrets than anyone in that room."
				<<case "docile">>
					"I think they all have secrets," you say. "You probably have some too, don't you?"
				<<case "flamboyant">>
					You say, "Everyone at that party seems to have a secret. I'm sure you've got a few of your own."
				<<case "cruel">>
					You say, "They're all hiding something, and so are you. I doubt you're any better than the rest of them."
				<<default>>
					You say, "Everyone in that room is hiding something. You probably are too."
			<</switch>>
			<br><br>
			Luchifen laughs, apparently amused by your accusation. "Of course I have secrets. Did you really expect me to tell you everything?"
	<</switch>>
	<<set $phase to 0>>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Arcology Party End 2]]>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<exit>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Party End 3]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Party End 2
<<effects>>
<<set _ptRemark to false>>
<<if $xchange.arcology.party.stepIn>><<set _ptRemark to true>>
		<<if $xchange.arcology.trouble and $xchange.arcology.trouble.source is "patron">>
			"I heard about what happened with the waiter," Luchifen says.
			They take your hand and turn it over, looking at your knuckles before letting go.
			"I heard about the threat too. That patron has already sent people downstairs to look for you."
			<br><br>
			They glance towards the balcony door, then turn back to you.
			"I'll arrange for someone to take you back to the hotel. Don't wander around on your own afterwards. Those people might still be looking for you when the party ends."
		<<else>>
			"Oh, and I heard about the waiter," Luchifen says.
			<br><br>
			They don't explain who told them, but they seem to know what happened.
			"You've upset one of the patrons tonight. Don't worry, I'll have a word with the patron. I'd rather you enjoy the rest of your visit without somebody causing you trouble."
		<</if>>
		<br><br>
		You can't tell whether Luchifen is pleased with what you did or annoyed that they had to get involved.
		<<if $xchange.arcology.party.status isnot "done">><<npcincr Luchifen love 1>><<glove>><</if>>
		<br><br>
	<</if>>
	<<if $xchange.arcology.party.seen.includes("nosy")>><<set _ptRemark to true>>
		<<if $xchange.arcology.trouble and $xchange.arcology.trouble.source is "guest">>
			"You were told to stop asking questions, weren't you?" Luchifen asks.
			<br><br>
			They don't wait for your answer.
			<br><br>
			"Next time, listen when someone asks to be left alone." They glance towards the party inside.
			"I'll make sure you get back to the hotel tonight. After that, be careful about anyone following you. I'd rather spend tomorrow doing something other than apologising for you."
			<<if $xchange.arcology.party.status isnot "done">><<npcincr Luchifen love -2>><<lllove>><</if>>
		<<else>>
			"Oh, the guest in the silver mask came to speak to me," Luchifen says, smiling.
			<br><br>
			"Apparently you were asking about the life before. I said you were new here and didn't know any better."
			They turn towards you, resting their back against the railing.
			"Ask me next time. I'm much better at making up answers, and you'll be less likely to upset anyone."
		<</if>>
		<br><br>
	<</if>>
	<<if !$xchange.arcology.party.xchanged>><<set _ptRemark to true>>
		"There's something else you should remember," Luchifen adds.
		"You came to the party looking like yourself. Some of the guests may recognise you if they see you on the mainland."
		<br><br>
		They smile slightly. "That's one of the reasons people use X-Change here. It's much easier to enjoy yourself when nobody knows who you really are later."
		<br><br>
	<</if>>
	<<if !_ptRemark>>
		Luchifen is quiet for a while, watching the lights of the city below.
		<br><br>
	<</if>>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Party End 3]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Party End 3
<<effects>>
<<if $worn.face.name is "white half-mask" and clothingIsBorrowed($worn.face)>><<faceundress "wardrobe">><</if>>
<<set _ambush to $xchange.arcology.party.status isnot "done" and setup.arcology.partyAmbush()>>
<<if $xchange.arcology.party.status isnot "done">>
	Luchifen turns towards the balcony door. "Well, thank you for coming. I hope you enjoyed yourself."
	<br><br>
	They open the door for you, waiting until you have stepped inside before following. The party is still going on, with guests talking around the tables and staff moving between them.
	<br><br>
	They gesture towards the doors leading out of the party. "You're welcome to come back. Just ask for the launch at the docks when you want to visit again."
	<<set $phase to 0>>
	<<set $xchange.arcology.party.status to "done">>
	<<set $xchange.arcology.outcome to "success">>
	<<if $xchange.arcology.redeem.stage is "invited">><<set $xchange.arcology.redeem.stage to "done">><<unset $xchange.arcology.redeem.boutWon, $xchange.arcology.redeem.sponsored>><</if>>
	/* Sponsorship covers one crossing's length plus a day's grace. */
	<<set $xchange.arcology.guest to { status: "sponsored", sponsor: "Luchifen", until: Time.date.timeStamp + (setup.arcology.voyageHours() + 24) * 3600 }>>
	<br><br>
	<span class="gold">You can now take the launch to the island from the docks.</span>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<set _endTarget to _ambush ? "Arcology Party Ambush" : "Arcology Hotel Room">>
<<if !_ambush>>
	You take the lift down from the party and return along Relay Street to the Hotel Meridian. The clerk looks up as you cross the lobby, then turns back to the desk screen. Upstairs, your room door recognises your implant and opens, shutting out the noise from the corridor once you're inside.
	<br><br>
<</if>>
<<link [[Next|_endTarget]]>><<pass 20>><<if _ambush>><<arcologyNPC 1 "vip" "merchant">><<else>><<endevent>><</if>><<unset $xchange.arcology.party.seen, $xchange.arcology.party.stepIn, $xchange.arcology.party.xchanged, $xchange.arcology.party.why, $xchange.arcology.party.openNotified, $xchange.arcology.party.blunders, $xchange.arcology.party.nosy, $xchange.arcology.party.back>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Party Failed
<<if $worn.face.name is "white half-mask" and clothingIsBorrowed($worn.face)>><<faceundress "wardrobe">><</if>>
<<effects>><<endevent>><<npc Luchifen>>
<<switch $xchange.arcology.party.why>>
<<case "refused">>
	Luchifen looks at the masks in their hands before putting them away. They take a moment to fold the ribbons around each mask, then slip them into their pocket.
<<case "left">>
	You reach the lift and press the button. When the doors open, you find Luchifen standing inside. They step out before you can enter, stopping in front of you.
<<case "departed">>
	You are halfway down the pier when you notice someone waiting beside the launch. As you get closer, you recognise Luchifen, who has apparently arrived before you.
<<case "missed">>
	You wait nearby. Before long, Luchifen comes to find you, still wearing their coat from the party. They stop a few steps away and take off their mask.
<<default>>
	The ballroom doors close behind you. You hear footsteps coming from behind and turn to find Luchifen approaching. They have taken off their mask.
<</switch>>
<br><br>
Luchifen looks at you quietly for a moment. Their usual smile is gone, and when they finally speak, they sound disappointed.
"I wanted you at the party. I made time for you tonight, you know. If you didn't want to come, you could have told me before we travelled all this way."
<br><br>
"Can I at least explain?" you ask.
<br><br>
Luchifen raises a hand to stop you, but lowers it after a moment. They seem to consider letting you speak before shaking their head.
"No need. I'll arrange for someone to take you home."
<<if $xchange.arcology.party.status isnot "failed">><<npcincr Luchifen love -5>><<llllove>><<set $xchange.arcology.party.status to "failed">><</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Expelled]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Expelled
<<effects>><<endevent>>
<<if $xchange.arcology.outcome isnot "failed">>
<<set $xchange.arcology.party.status to "failed">>
<<set $xchange.arcology.outcome to "failed">>
<<set $xchange.arcology.guest to { status: "revoked", sponsor: "", until: 0 }>>
<<set $xchange.arcology.redeem.stage to "silent">>
<<unset $xchange.arcology.redeem.boutWon, $xchange.arcology.redeem.sponsored>>
<<set $xchange.arcology.shun to { day: Time.days, rollDay: -1, ready: false }>>
<<unset $xchange.arcology.trouble>>
<</if>>
When you turn around, you find two people in plain grey suits standing a few steps behind you. You hadn't heard them coming, and Luchifen doesn't even look in their direction.
<br><br>
A notice appears in your holographic display.
<br><br>
<<holo "CIVIC REGISTRY / NOTICE" "denied">>
	<<holoRow "GUEST" `$xchange.arcology.handle`>>
	<<holoRow "SPONSOR" "WITHDRAWN">>
	<<holoLine "GUEST AUTHORIZATION REVOKED" "denied">>
<</holo>>
<br>
"See <<phim>> home," Luchifen says to the two people before turning and walking away.
<br><br>
One of them steps closer and takes hold of your arm, just above the elbow. The other moves to your opposite side, while the first begins leading you away.
<br><br>
<<link [[Walk with them|Arcology Expelled 2]]>><<set $phase to "walk">><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Refuse to move|Arcology Expelled 2]]>><<set $phase to "refuse">><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Expelled 2
<<location "arcology_pier">><<effects>>
<<if $phase is "refuse">>
	You refuse to walk any further. The two look at each other before one of them grabs you under your arms while the other lifts your legs off the ground. Together, they carry you down to the pier, ignoring your refusal.
	<br><br>
	People move out of their way as they pass. A few turn to look at you, but quickly return to what they were doing. The two don't hurt you, but they don't put you down either, leaving you with no choice but to be carried along.
	<<stress 6>><<gstress>><<trauma 4>><<gtrauma>>
<<else>>
		You walk between the two of them towards the white pier. <<if $xchange.arcology.party.why isnot "departed">>They lead you along Relay Street, where people move aside to let you pass before returning to what they were doing.<<else>>They keep hold of your arm for the rest of the walk down the pier.<</if>> Even the guards at the gate let the three of you pass.
	<<stress 3>><<gstress>>
<</if>>
<<set $phase to 0>>
<br><br>
A small grey boat is waiting at the end of the pier, with its engine already running.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Voyage Board]]>><<set $xchange.arcology.voyage to { to: "town", escort: "loyalists", next: "Docks" }>><<unset $xchange.arcology.party.seen, $xchange.arcology.party.stepIn, $xchange.arcology.party.xchanged, $xchange.arcology.party.why, $xchange.arcology.party.openNotified, $xchange.arcology.party.blunders, $xchange.arcology.party.nosy, $xchange.arcology.party.back>><<pass 3>><</link>>
<br>

/* REDEMPTION */
:: Arcology Shun
<<set $outside to 1>><<set $location to "docks">><<effects>>
<<arcologyShunCheck>>
<<if $xchange.arcology.shun.ready>>
	<<include "Arcology Reconcile">>
<<else>>
	<<set $xchange.arcology.shun.ignored to ($xchange.arcology.shun.ignored or 0) + 1>>
	<<set $xchange.arcology.umbrella to true>><<arcologyVictorPronouns>>
	You walk towards the railing by the water, where you spoke to Luchifen before. They are standing in the same place, but this time someone else is with them. A tall <<print _vman>> in a dark coat stands beside Luchifen, holding a black umbrella above their head<<if Weather.precipitation is "none">>, even though it isn't raining<</if>>.
	<br><br>
	<<if $xchange.arcology.shun.ignored is 1>>
		You call Luchifen's name, hoping to get their attention. They turn towards you and seem to recognise you immediately, but say nothing before looking back at the sea.
		<br><br>
		The <<print _vman>> beside them doesn't even turn towards you. <<print _vHe>> simply adjusts the umbrella to keep it above Luchifen's head, showing no interest in your presence.
	<<elseif $xchange.arcology.shun.ignored is 2>>
		You approach Luchifen and try to apologise, but they take a phone out of their coat while you're speaking. They begin reading something on the screen, completely ignoring what you're saying.
		<br><br>
		You continue for a little longer, hoping they'll at least respond, but eventually give up when they show no sign of listening.
	<<else>>
		<<switch random(1, 3)>>
		<<case 1>>
			You stand beside Luchifen for a while, hoping they'll speak to you. Instead, they continue watching a cargo ship approaching the docks, paying no attention to you.
			<br><br>
			You wait until the ship has stopped and been tied in place, but Luchifen still hasn't said anything. They finally turn away and walk along the docks without looking back. The <<print _vman>> follows beside them, keeping the umbrella above Luchifen's head.
		<<case 2>>
			Luchifen glances at you briefly, and their expression seems to change for a moment. Before you can tell what they're thinking, the <<print _vman>> beside them leans closer and says something too quietly for you to hear.
			<br><br>
			Luchifen gives a small nod before turning their attention back to the sea, leaving you standing there without an answer.
		<<default>>
			You call Luchifen's name, hoping they'll at least look at you. The <<print _vman>> turns towards you briefly, but says nothing.
			<br><br>
			Luchifen continues looking out at the sea, ignoring you completely.
		<</switch>>
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave them alone|Docks]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Arcology Reconcile
<<endevent>><<npc Luchifen>><<arcologyVictorPronouns>>
The <<print _vman>> holding the umbrella is still standing beside Luchifen. As you approach, <<print _vhe>> looks at Luchifen, who gives a small nod without looking away from the sea. The <<print _vman>> lowers the umbrella and walks farther down the docks, stopping where <<print _vhe>> won't be able to hear your conversation.
<br><br>
Luchifen remains by the railing, watching the water as you come closer.
<br><br>
"I wondered when you'd try again," they say, looking towards you. They move slightly to one side, giving you room to stand beside them.
<br><br>
"I was angry with you. I still am, a little." They turn towards you. "I went to a lot of trouble arranging that visit, only for you to walk away. If I'm going to invite you again, I'd like to know you won't do the same thing."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Reconcile 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Reconcile 2
<<effects>>
"So, I've decided to give you another chance, but there's something I want you to do first." Luchifen smiles, apparently enjoying the idea. "Become the champion of the underground Colosseum, and perhaps I'll invite you back."
<br><br>
"Why the arena?" you ask.
<br><br>
"Because I've heard plenty of promises from people standing right here, and I'd rather see what you can actually do." They lean against the railing. "Besides, I think I'd enjoy watching you fight. You could even wave to me up in the gallery, assuming you're still speaking to me by then."
<br><br>
"Are you joking?" you ask.
<br><br>
"About waving to me? Of course." Luchifen chuckles. "But I do want you to win that championship. I'll be waiting to hear about it."
<<set $xchange.arcology.redeem.stage to "arena">><<unset $xchange.arcology.shun>>
<br><br>
<<if setup.arcology.arenaQualified()>>
	<<link [[Tell them you already are|Arcology Redeem Report]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<<elseif setup.arcology.arenaBlocked()>>
	<<link [[Say the arena won't let you|Arcology Redeem Blocked]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Docks]]>><<endevent>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Redeem Blocked
<<effects>><<set _arcologyCol to $xchange.colosseum>>
You explain why you can't fight at the Colosseum anymore.
<<if _arcologyCol.banUntil gt Time.date.timeStamp>>
	You've been banned, so you can't sign up for another fight until the ban ends.
<<elseif ["walked", "disrupted"].includes(_arcologyCol.ending)>>
	The Colosseum won't let you fight there anymore because of how things ended last time.
<<else>>
	You were offered a championship fight before, but you didn't take it. The Colosseum won't give you another chance.
<</if>>
<br><br>
"I know." Luchifen doesn't sound surprised. "I watch the board." They take out their phone, but don't unlock it yet. "So you can't do it their way. Then you'll do it mine."
<br><br>
"Just one match against their strongest fighter, with everyone watching." They smile at you. "If you win, I'll accept that. If you lose, I'll arrange another match for you."
<br><br>
They look down at their phone, smiling to themselves. "Of course, the more times you lose, the more people will get to watch you try."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Redeem Blocked 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Redeem Blocked 2
<<effects>>
Luchifen makes a call while you stand beside them. You can't hear the person on the other end, but Luchifen seems to know exactly who to speak to.
"I'd like to arrange a special match. Yes, against your S-rank fighter."
<br><br>
They listen to the reply before continuing. "Under my name, please. You can keep the existing restrictions. This match will be arranged separately, and I'll cover the cost."
<br><br>
After a short conversation, Luchifen ends the call and puts their phone away. "You can ask about your match at the fighters' desk later. They're expecting you."
<<set $xchange.arcology.redeem.sponsored to true>><<set $xchange.colosseum.luchifenBout to 1>>
<br><br>
<span class="gold">Luchifen has arranged an S-rank match for you at the Colosseum.</span> Ask about it at the fighters' desk.
<<if $xchange.colosseum.debt gt 0>>
	<span class="red">You still owe the Colosseum money.</span>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Docks]]>><<endevent>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Redeem Report
<<effects>>
<<if $xchange.arcology.redeem.boutWon>>
	"I saw the whole thing," Luchifen says, smiling. "You could have saved me the worry and finished it sooner."
<<elseif $xchange.colosseum.ending is "inside">>
	You tell them that you've become the house champion and even managed to visit the upstairs rooms.
	<br><br>
	"Oh, I know," they say, looking rather pleased. "The house champion, and you've even been reading their books. You've been quite busy, haven't you? I only asked you to win."
<<else>>
	You tell them that you've become the house champion.
	<br><br>
	"I know. I watched some of your fights," they say with a smile. "Although I'd have been rather surprised if you'd lost."
<</if>>
<br><br>
They smile at you more openly than they have since you left the island. "Well, you did what I asked, so it's only fair that I keep my promise."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Redeem Report 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Redeem Report 2
<<effects>>
Luchifen touches the small light behind their ear before continuing.
<br><br>
"Your handle still exists. I've had your access restored, so you can visit again." They smile. "There will be another party soon, and you'll come to it this time, won't you?"
<<if $xchange.arcology.redeem.stage is "arena">><<npcincr Luchifen love 3>><<ggglove>><</if>>
<<set $xchange.arcology.redeem.stage to "invited">>
<br><br>
<<link [[Go with them now|Arcology Return Board]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Not today|Docks]]>><<endevent>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Return Board
<<effects>>
"Then let's not waste the tide," Luchifen says, and walks you down to the black launch at the end of the docks.
<br><br>
<<link [[Board the launch|Arcology Voyage Board]]>><<set $xchange.arcology.voyage to { to: "arcology", escort: "luchifen", next: "Arcology Return Arrival", talked: true }>><<endevent>><<pass 3>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Return Arrival
<<location "arcology_pier">><<effects>><<endevent>><<npc Luchifen>>
<<if $xchange.arcology.guest.status isnot "sponsored">>
	<<run setup.arcology.scheduleParty()>>
	<<set $xchange.arcology.guest to { status: "sponsored", sponsor: "Luchifen", until: $xchange.arcology.party.end + 10 * 3600 }>>
	<<set $xchange.arcology.outcome to "">>
<</if>>
The launch arrives back at the white pier. Two guards in grey armour stand beside the security scanner, watching the passengers as they arrive. You follow Luchifen to the glass booth, where the clerk looks up when you approach.
<br><br>
This time, the clerk doesn't ask you to register as a guest.
<br><br>
<<holo "CIVIC REGISTRY">>
	<<holoRow "HANDLE" `$xchange.arcology.handle`>>
	<<holoRow "SPONSOR" "LUCHIFEN">>
	<<holoRow "PREVIOUS STATUS" "REVOKED">>
	<<holoLine "AUTHORIZATION RENEWED" "ok">>
<</holo>>
<br>
Your permission to stay on the island has been restored. Luchifen checks the information before turning to you.
"You'll be staying in the same room. The rules haven't changed, either. The party is <<print setup.arcology.when($xchange.arcology.party.at)>> at the Glasshouse. I'll meet you by the lift an hour before it starts."
<br><br>
Luchifen starts walking away, but stops after a few steps and looks back at you. "Oh, and <<arcologyHandle>>? I'm glad you came back."
<br><br>
They smile briefly before continuing on their way, leaving you wondering whether they were being sincere.
<br><br>
<<link [[Go to the hotel|Arcology Hotel]]>><<endevent>><<pass 10>><</link>>
<br>
